                                    <div class="column-bg-overlay-wrap" data-bg-animation="none">
                                       <div class="column-bg-overlay"></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="wpb_wrapper"></div>
                                 </div>
                              </div>
                              <div class="vc_col-sm-5 wpb_column column_container vc_column_container col no-extra-padding inherit_tablet inherit_phone " data-t-w-inherits="default" data-bg-cover="" data-padding-pos="all" data-has-bg-color="false" data-bg-color="" data-bg-opacity="1" data-hover-bg="" data-hover-bg-opacity="1" data-animation="" data-delay="0">
                                 <div class="vc_column-inner">
                                    <div class="column-bg-overlay-wrap" data-bg-animation="none">
                                       <div class="column-bg-overlay"></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                       <div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
                                          <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                             <p style="text-align: center;"><span class="white bold fs22">Many people think of Tarot as a party trick. A bit of frivolous fun to peer into the future.</span></p>
                                             <p style="text-align: center;"><span class="white bold fs22">But I see things differently.</span></p>
                                             <p style="text-align: center;"><span class="white bold fs22">You see, Tarot isn't about predicting your future. It's about creating your future.</span></p>
                                          </div>
                                       </div>
                                    </div>
                                 </div>
                              </div>
                           </div>
                        </div>
                        <div id="fws_5ef418ba76338" data-column-margin="default" data-midnight="dark" class="wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_row standard_section " style="padding-top: 50px; padding-bottom: 50px; ">
                           <div class="row-bg-wrap" data-bg-animation="none" data-bg-overlay="false">
                              <div class="inner-wrap">
                                 <div class="row-bg" style=""></div>
                              </div>
                              <div class="row-bg-overlay"></div>
                           </div>
                           <div class="row_col_wrap_12 col span_12 dark left">
                              <div class="vc_col-sm-12 vc_col-lg-offset-2 vc_col-lg-8 vc_col-md-offset-2 vc_col-md-8 wpb_column column_container vc_column_container col no-extra-padding inherit_tablet inherit_phone " data-t-w-inherits="default" data-bg-cover="" data-padding-pos="all" data-has-bg-color="false" data-bg-color="" data-bg-opacity="1" data-hover-bg="" data-hover-bg-opacity="1" data-animation="" data-delay="0">
                                 <div class="vc_column-inner">
                                    <div class="column-bg-overlay-wrap" data-bg-animation="none">
                                       <div class="column-bg-overlay"></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                       <div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
                                          <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                             <h2 class="center purple fs34 bold">Tarot is the Mirror To Your Soul</h2>
                                          </div>
                                       </div>
                                       <div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
                                          <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                             <p>And every card is an invitation to go deep within and connect your daily life with your Divine purpose.</p>
                                             <p>Think you're not &#8216;psychic' enough to read Tarot? Think again.</p>
                                             <p>I believe that everyone is intuitive &#8211; including YOU.</p>
                                             <p>All you need to do is say YES to your intuition. It's that simple.</p>
                                             <p>And through the practice of reading Tarot, you'll deepen your connection with your intuition even further, which means more clarity, more purpose, and more joy in your life.</p>
                                          </div>
                                       </div>
                                       <div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
                                          <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                             <p style="text-align: center;"><span class="darkgreen bold fs22">If you're ready to trust your intuition and manifest your future, with Tarot as your guide,<a href="">click here</a> and choose the path that resonates with you.</span></p>
                                          </div>
                                       </div>
                                    </div>
                                 </div>
                              </div>
                           </div>
                        </div>
                        <div id="fws_5ef418ba76968" data-column-margin="default" data-midnight="dark" data-bg-mobile-hidden="true" class="wpb_row vc_row-fluid vc_row full-width-section standard_section " style="padding-top: 0px; padding-bottom: 0px; ">
                           <div class="row-bg-wrap" data-bg-animation="none" data-bg-overlay="true">
                              <div class="inner-wrap using-image">
                                 <div class="row-bg using-image" style="background-image: url(https://www.biddytarot.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/About_BG-3.jpg); background-position: right top; background-repeat: no-repeat; "></div>
                              </div>
                              <div class="row-bg-overlay" style="background: #faf4f4; background: linear-gradient(90deg,#faf4f4 0%,rgba(0,0,0,0.01) 100%);  opacity: 0.95; "></div>
                           </div>
                           <div class="row_col_wrap_12 col span_12 dark left">
                              <div class="vc_col-sm-12 vc_col-lg-8 vc_col-md-6 wpb_column column_container vc_column_container col no-extra-padding inherit_tablet inherit_phone " data-t-w-inherits="default" data-bg-cover="" data-padding-pos="all" data-has-bg-color="false" data-bg-color="" data-bg-opacity="1" data-hover-bg="" data-hover-bg-opacity="1" data-animation="" data-delay="0">
                                 <div class="vc_column-inner">
                                    <div class="column-bg-overlay-wrap" data-bg-animation="none">
                                       <div class="column-bg-overlay"></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                       <div class="divider-wrap" data-alignment="default">
                                          <div style="height: 75px;" class="divider"></div>
                                       </div>
                                       <div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
                                          <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                             <h2 class="center green fs34 bold">How I Started with Tarot</h2>
                                          </div>
                                       </div>
                                       <div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element ">
                                          <div class="wpb_wrapper">
                                             <p>It all started in an old musty room above a new age store in Sydney.  I was 17 and about to head off on a school exchange to Germany and wanted to know what would happen on the trip.</p>
                                             <p>I walked up the creaky wooden stairs into a room filled with crystals, angels and incense and sat down for a Tarot reading.</p>
                                             <p>“Ooh, the Emperor! You’re going to find love!&#8221; cooed the Tarot reader, who was dressed in a head scarf and dark eyeliner. I brushed it off, thinking that she was just telling me what I wanted to hear. But, six months later, I had fallen madly in love with a boy in Germany.</p>
                                             <p style="text-align: center;"><span class="yellow bold fs22">I was intrigued! I had to figure out a way to tap into this powerful mystical tool.</span></p>
                                             <p>I bought every Tarot book I could find and begged my mum to buy me my first Tarot deck. And then, I studied like crazy. Keyword charts. Cheat sheets. And LOTS of memorisation. (Heck, if it worked for my University studies, surely it'd work for my Tarot studies.)</p>
                                             <p>But, there was just one problem. Every time I went to read the Tarot cards, I felt stressed about remembering the card meanings and whether I was doing it right. Worse, my readings felt robotic and dull – not exactly the cosmic download from the Universe that I had hoped for.</p>
                                             <p style="text-align: center;"><span class="yellow bold fs22">I studied harder and harder, praying I would eventually &#8216;master' the Tarot. But it didn't help.</span></p>
                                             <p>Until one day, I finally realised, reading Tarot is NOT about memorising the cards and following the book.</p>
                                             <p>It's about trusting your intuition &#8211; and letting the cards guide you to the answers you need.</p>
                                             <p>From that day on, the way I read Tarot changed dramatically.</p>
                                             <p>Instead of <em>thinking</em> what a card meant, I <em>felt</em> what it meant to <em>me.</em></p>
                                             <p style="text-align: center;"><span class="yellow bold fs22">And instead of worrying about the right meaning for a card, I let the imagery and symbolism of the card guide me.</span></p>
                                             <p>I had finally discovered that blissful place where Tarot just <em>flows</em>. And now, I show my students how to do the same in <a href="">my Tarot courses and programs</a>.</p>
                                          </div>
                                       </div>
                                       <div class="divider-wrap" data-alignment="default">
                                          <div style="height: 75px;" class="divider"></div>
                                       </div>
                                       <div class="img-with-aniamtion-wrap center" data-max-width="100%" data-max-width-mobile="default" data-border-radius="none" data-shadow="none" data-animation="fade-in">
                                          <div class="inner">
                                             <div class="hover-wrap" data-hover-animation="none">
                                                <div class="hover-wrap-inner"> <img class="img-with-animation skip-lazy mobileshow" data-delay="0" height="1032" width="718" data-animation="fade-in" src="https://www.biddytarot.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/About_BG-3_mobile.jpg" alt="" srcset="https://www.biddytarot.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/About_BG-3_mobile.jpg 718w, https://www.biddytarot.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/About_BG-3_mobile-334x480.jpg 334w, https://www.biddytarot.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/About_BG-3_mobile-300x431.jpg 300w" sizes="(min-width: 1450px) 75vw, (min-width: 1000px) 85vw, 100vw" /></div>
                                             </div>
